        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: વાવાઝોડું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વાવાઝોડું — vāvājhoḍũ — \"a cyclone\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ગઈકાલે રાત્રે દરિયા કિનારે મોટું વાવાઝોડું આવ્યું. gaīkāle rātre dariyā kināre moṭũ vāvājhoḍũ āvyũ. Last night a big cyclone hit the coast."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is probably built on vā, wind, which CDIAL lists for Gujarati under Sanskrit vāyú, \"wind\" (CDIAL 11544); no dictionary we use records the rest of the word, so its history is not settled. It is neuter, and it આવે છે, comes: વાવાઝોડું (vāvājhoḍũ) આવ્યું. તોફાન is any storm; a વાવાઝોડું (vāvājhoḍũ) is a whirling one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
