              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "goes back to Sanskrit chattvará, \"a house, a bower\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati noun, \"a thatched roof, a cottage\" (CDIAL 4976). છત is a ceiling or a flat roof; a છાપરું (chāprũ) is a sloping roof of thatch or tiles."
